# Trivy findings accepted with a documented reason. Keep this list short and
# justified — an unexplained entry here is how a real finding gets buried.

# DS-0002 — "Image user should not be 'root'".
# opengym/Dockerfile intentionally has no final USER instruction. The container
# must start as root for three things only, all in the entrypoint before any
# server starts: chown the Supervisor-managed /data (whose ownership we do not
# control), create /run/opengym 0700 for the api's internal socket, and render
# the nginx template. It then runs EVERY long-running process — the gateway,
# nginx and the openGym api — as the unprivileged `app` user (uid 1000) via
# gosu, with HOME=/home/app (docs/contract.md §1), and fails loudly if /data is
# not writable as that user. Only the supervising shell that forwards signals
# stays root. Same model as the myMeal/HomeHoard add-ons.
DS-0002
